From 8a21a4b3053b5decc2827861262fd55ad596e445 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:42:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/36] B70-K2-0001: split the packed full-attention KV bucket
 (QSA), env-gated

On the sparse (QSA) engine the trunk packs all 12 full-attention layers and
their 12 compressed-key caches into one KV group, so every block is 10.9 MB and
each small per-request state group (GDN x(2+K), PLE short conv, QSA ring,
DFlash SWA) pays whole fat blocks: ~425 MiB per running request vs ~287 MiB on
dense, -32 % free KV at 6 running.

B70_KV_SPLIT_GROUPS=1 lowers the repeat floor of the balanced mixed-page
bucket to 1 (66 groups, 905,216 B blocks); B70_KV_PACK_REPEATS=<n> sets n
explicitly and wins. Both unset = upstream packing (default off). Split groups
pair full_i with its own side caches by layer index, not dict order.

CPU: tests/v1/core/test_b70_kv_pack_repeats.py (6 env cases x 5 shuffled
orders: partition, per-layer pairing, group count, bytes per block).
test_kv_cache_utils.py failure set unchanged vs HEAD (49 pre-existing).
